The numpy brains now detect the version of the installed numpy in a single place
and describe the matching numpy API, instead of repeating ad hoc version checks.
Versions are compared as numbers, so numpy 1.9 is no longer mistaken for a version
that supports subscripting scalar types; the version is read from the distribution
metadata instead of importing numpy; and the most recent API is assumed when numpy
is not installed.

Refs #2710
